      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BRIEF AUTHORITY (3) made very nice improvement from his first campaign to then be winning first up at Grafton. There would be no reason he can't go on with it now coming off a six week break. Maybe he needs to be kept fresh and that happens here. KIRRA'S SISTER (2) is a very consistent mare who likes to lead but struggles to hang on. This is the easiest race she has been in for a little while. AMAYA'S SECRET (1) is never beaten far at all. From the gate, she can land behind the speed and try to pounce late. TRYANZA (7) has been out of the money in recent runs including last time out when sixth over 1120m at Lismore two weeks ago. Has placed on the going and can contest.",
